<title>USA: INTERVIEW--U.S. Office backs EPS estimate.</title>
<headline>INTERVIEW--U.S. Office backs EPS estimate.</headline>
<byline>Brendan Intindola</byline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Office Products Co's chairman and CEO strongly backed Wall Street's earnings forecasts for the company Thursday, emphasizing the non-dilutive nature of U.S. Office's stock-swap purchase of Mail Boxes Etc announced this morning.</p>
<p>Jonathan Ledecky told Reuters in an interview that he is &quot;supremely confident&quot; U.S. Office's earnings for the fourth quarter and 1997 fiscal year ended last month will reach the analysts' consensus views of $0.30 and $1.20 per share, repectively.</p>
</text>
